--- !u!114 &4362864536158133381
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "If an object is not affected by a hand-placed Reflection Probe, it will automatically receive reflections from the Sky. Therefore, placing local Reflection Probes in each room of the template is required to avoid a phenomenon called \u201Clight leaking\u201D, and prevent the sky from affecting areas that would normally be occluded.\r\n\n1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> expand <b>Lighting</b> > <b>Reflection Probes.</b>\r\n\r\n2. Disable the <b>Room2</b> GameObject which contains all the local <b>Reflection Probes</b> for this room.\n\r\nYou can see that if the local <b>Reflection Probes</b> in this room are disabled, the sky is automatically reflected onto all objects, and therefore it creates unwanted light leaking.\r\n\nReflection Probes can have two types of shape:\n\u2022 A <b>Box</b> is useful for setting up reflections for an indoor environment like a room.\n\u2022 A <b>Sphere</b> may be more suited for an open outdoor environment."
